apt 2.7.14 apt-pkg: tolerate missing dpkg tuple/cputable tables on OHOS

pkgInitArchTupleMap() loads dpkg's cputable/tupletable/triplettable from
DPKG_DATADIR to build the architecture<->tuple mapping used for
multi-arch.  On OHOS/musl there is no dpkg data directory and no
cputable, so the open fails and the whole library initialization fails
with an I/O error before any client can start.

Verified on the OHOS build host:

  $ ls /usr/share/dpkg/cputable
  ls: /usr/share/dpkg/cputable: No such file or directory

Fix: when the cputable cannot be opened, degrade to an empty
ArchToTupleMap and return success (architecture matching falls back to
plain name comparison against APT::Architecture).  On Debian systems the
tables exist and this branch is inert.
--- a/apt-pkg/init.cc
+++ b/apt-pkg/init.cc
@@ -63,6 +63,14 @@
    // Load a list of CPUs
    std::vector<std::string> cpus;
    std::ifstream cputable(cpupath);
+   if (cputable.is_open() == false)
+   {
+      // OHOS/musl 环境通常没有 dpkg 数据目录（DPKG_DATADIR），架构->tuple
+      // 映射表（cputable/tupletable）不存在。退化处理：保留空 ArchToTupleMap，
+      // 架构匹配退化为按名字的直接匹配（APT::Architecture），而不是让整个
+      // 库初始化失败。
+      return true;
+   }
    for (std::string cpuline; std::getline(cputable, cpuline); )
    {
